// ============================================================================
// dns-queries.spl — DNS Log Analysis (Splunk SIEM Homelab)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Queries as executed in Splunk Enterprise against index="homelab".
// Each query is preserved exactly as documented; run one block at a time.
// ============================================================================


// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Query 1: Most frequently queried domain names
// Purpose: Establish a baseline of expected DNS destinations and surface
//          any domain that dominates traffic.
// Observed: 1,200 events; google.com 139, printer.local 139, example.com 137 ...
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

index="homelab" source="dns_logs.json"
| stats count by query
| sort - count


// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Query 2: Most active source IPs generating DNS traffic
// Purpose: Profile per-client DNS volume to isolate noisy or compromised hosts.
// Observed: 2,400 events across 12 source hosts; top host 192.168.1.10 (226).
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

index="homelab" sourcetype="_json"
| stats count by id.orig_h
| sort - count


// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Query 3: Breakdown of DNS query types (A, AAAA, CNAME, PTR)
// Purpose: Baseline the record-type mix so abnormal types (TXT/NULL used in
//          DNS tunneling) become recognizable.
// Observed: A 526, AAAA 642, CNAME 514, PTR 618 (2,400 events).
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

index="homelab" sourcetype="_json"
| stats count by qtype


// ============================================================================
// OPTIONAL IMPROVEMENTS — NOT EXECUTED, NO EVIDENCE CAPTURED
// Suggested refinements for future work. Clearly different from the tested
// queries above: they have not been run and produce no documented results.
// ============================================================================

// Improvement A: standardize the sourcetype filter.
// Queries 2 and 3 use the broad sourcetype="_json" filter, while Query 1 uses
// source="dns_logs.json". If the DNS data has (or is given) its own sourcetype,
// all three queries should use it consistently to avoid pulling in unrelated
// JSON events from the same index.

// index="homelab" sourcetype="dns_logs"
// | stats count by query
// | sort - count


// Improvement B: prioritize rare domains instead of only the most frequent.
// Frequency hunting usually matters at the bottom of the list (possible DGA /
// beaconing), not the top.

// index="homelab" source="dns_logs.json"
// | stats count by query
// | sort + count
